"Usage: /watch chat_id  •  /unwatch chat_id  •  /readlog chat_id": "",
"✨ <b>Welcome, {first_name}!</b>\n<blockquote>Glad to have you in <b>{chat_name}</b> 💫\nBe kind and enjoy your stay 🌸</blockquote>": "",
"👋 <b>Goodbye, {first_name}</b>\n<blockquote>See you again in <b>{chat_name}</b> 💫</blockquote>": "",
"👋 <b>Welcome guide 1/3: the basics</b>\n<blockquote>/setwelcome your text sets the message.\nSend a photo with /setwelcome as caption to add a picture.\n/welcome on or off turns it on or off.\n/resetwelcome goes back to the default.\n/cleanwelcome on deletes the old welcome when a new one comes.</blockquote>\n<b>Fillings</b> are words in curly brackets that change per person:\n<blockquote>{first} first name\n{last} last name\n{fullname} both names\n{username} @username, or name if none\n{mention} a tap-able name\n{id} their id\n{chatname} group name</blockquote>Example: <code>/setwelcome Hi {first}, welcome to {chatname}!</code>\nShows: <i>Hi Asha, welcome to My Group!</i>": "",
"🎛 <b>Welcome guide 2/3: buttons</b>\n<blockquote>Format: [Text](buttonurl://link)\nPut it at the end of your welcome text.</blockquote>\n<b>Same row:</b> add <code>:same</code> to put a button beside the one before it.\n<b>Colours:</b> telegram allows only three, plus normal:\n<blockquote>:blue 🔵 main action\n:green 🟢 good or safe\n:red 🔴 warning\nno word = normal grey-tinted button</blockquote>Colours and :same can be combined in any order.\nOther colours (brown, purple...) are not possible, telegram decides.": "",
"✨ <b>Welcome guide 3/3: examples</b>\n<b>One blue button:</b>\n<code>Welcome {first}!\n[Our site](buttonurl://https://example.com:blue)</code>\n\n<b>Two buttons on one row:</b>\n<code>[Google](buttonurl://https://google.com:green)\n[Bing](buttonurl://https://bing.com:same:red)</code>\n\n<b>Random welcome</b> (bot picks one each time, split with %%%):\n<code>Hello {first}! %%% Hey {first}, glad you came! %%% Welcome {mention}!</code>\n\n<b>Extras:</b> {preview} shows link previews, {nonotif} sends silently, {protect} blocks forwarding, {mediaspoiler} hides the photo until tapped.": "",
